{
  "_note": "Three-day event at the Singapore Expo, 2026-09-04 to 2026-09-06 (dates from Riot's own preview article, \"All Eyes on Singapore\", 2026-08-23). Recorded under the Sunday date because that is when the top 8 standings were set — same convention as Barcelona. The results article is dated 2026-09-09, which is its PUBLICATION date and not the event date (§5); it says only \"this past weekend\". Riot published no attendance figure for this event. The Day 1 field is derivable as roughly 1,900 from the metagame table (218 Kennen at 11.5%) and Day 2 as roughly 300 (58 at 19.3%), but those are inferred rather than published, so player_count is left unset instead of storing a computed number. NOTE ON THE ARTICLE: its prose says the Top 8 held \"five Kennen, two Master Yi, Wuju Bladesman, and one Akali\". The decklists and their own Legend Rank fields disagree — Kennen ranks #1-#4 of 218 (four decks), Master Yi #1-#2 of 124, Akali #1/72, Fiora #1/54, totalling eight. The listings are used. Also note the article prints a long \"Best-of Decks\" section BEFORE the top 8, including three players who appear in both; the top 8 here is the final Overall Ranking #8-#1 run (§16). Cards are written as names exactly as published; the importer resolves each to its base printing.",
